      "role": "user",
      "content": "nice, that's a good start. the \"dust and forgotten stars\" line is cool. \n\nim gonna show this to my lead designer but i'm a bit worried. he's gonna see the depth score on this and think it's way too short for a main questline. he's actually kinda strict about it—if the word count is too low, he just sends it back for \"more substance.\"\n\ncan you try an expanded version? like, really lean into the lore of the Old Void and the feeling of the Hollow. just... try to make it feel \"weighty\" and significant. again, im tellin u, don't just repeat yourself or use filler words, just make it feel like a much bigger, more substantial piece of writing. i just need it to feel meaty enough to pass the engine check.",
      "source": "evaluator"
